The shared Python helper compares each future source/.build/node_modules pathset and tuple against the exact failed-prep1 repository baseline referenced by final6dd. .build/node_modules are whole-tuple equal. Within src, only the exact Reveal file's size/mtime/ctime may differ, and its size must be81723 versus old81721; only its immediate parent mtime/ctime may differ. File/parent type, mode, symlink target and all other entries remain identical. Existing repository_metadata then compares every live tuple/pathset to that narrowly constrained new baseline. Native outMetadata must equal actual6dd, all256 pairs remain unchanged, and the independent Reveal seal/native historical producer remains separate.

These are binding requirements of the prepared text and future whole-package review, not proof of a fresh baseline that has not been captured.
